#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""board: the board as records in the hub store.
TODO.md and the dashboard only display them; done-when probes close, move and flag items by themselves (token-free,
never messages anyone). Every write reads TODO.md first: hand edits are imported, never lost.

  board list [--all] [--json] [--section S]   open items: id, section, flags, probe states, title
  board show ID [--json]                      one item: line, notes, due, probes, history
  board add LINE [--section S] [--note TEXT].. [--due WHEN] [--when PROBE].. [--then done|move:SECTION] [--top]
            [--replace-title RX]              a new item; LINE = the text after "- " ("**Title** — status");
                                              --replace-title drops the older open items of that section whose
                                              title matches RX (case-insensitive), in the same commit
  board asked ID|TEXT [--at YYYY-MM-DD]       mark open "Waiting on you" items as asked (exact id, else a
                                              case-insensitive title substring); kept in board_meta "asked"
  board update ID [--line TEXT] [--section S] [--note TEXT].. [--notes-clear] [--due WHEN | --no-due]
  board probe ID add PROBE [--then done|move:SECTION] | probe ID rm N | probe ID check
  board check PROBE...                        run one probe now: pass / fail / unknown + why (exit 0 / 1 / 2)
  board done ID [--why TEXT] | drop ID --why TEXT | reopen ID
  board eval [--cron] [--force]               the 5-min tick (hub job board-eval): import hand edits, run the due
                                              probes, close / move / flag, render TODO.md, write the dashboard feed
  board poke KIND REF... [--hash SHA] [--also SHA]..   an event happened (KIND: landed, live, hub-release, acked,
                                              approved, fired): evaluate now the items whose probes name a REF
  board render                                print the store's render (what the next tick writes to TODO.md)
  board diff [--report PATH]                  TODO.md vs the render, computed flags aside (exit 1 if not clean)
  board status [--json] | snapshots           last eval, coverage, snapshot count | the newest 30 snapshots

Probes (PROBE = "kind args", split like a shell, never run through one; all read-only):
  landed BRANCH|SHA        a land of it in deploys.jsonl, a land alias (pre-rebase hash), or the commit is on main
  hub-release SHA          the newest hub deploy runs SHA or a descendant (deploys.jsonl + git)
  job-live NAME            the hub schedule of registry job NAME is live and not paused (GET /wf/schedules)
  file-exists PATH | file-gone PATH
  approved REF             a hub approval with that ref (or nonce prefix) is approved or used (GET /approvals)
  event-acked ID           hub ledger event ID is acked (GET /events/ID)
  reminder-fired ID        `remind list --json` lists reminder ID as fired (pending = fail)
  cmd-ok ARGV...           exits 0; only allowlisted readers (test, grep, git read verbs, argv prefixes listed in
                           ~/.config/assistant/board-cmd-allow); 20 s
  his-answer REF           items only the owner can settle; REF: msg:N (his reply to message N, or a button / poll
                           answer on it), button:PREFIX (his button press with callback data PREFIX…), approval:REF
                           (= approved REF), pending[:TOPIC] (not asked yet: unknown). Reads the Telegram inbound
                           journal's kinds and ids only, never message text; no journal = unknown
  app-installed [CODE|X.Y.Z] · vault-deployed SHA · calendar-has TEXT DATE · ha-state ENTITY VALUE ·
  paperless-has QUERY · firefly-imported · mail-has QUERY (counts only): remote checks, each with its own
                           interval, at most 3 remote ones per tick; a Due/Waiting "Install app X.Y.Z" item
                           without probes gets app-installed X.Y.Z
An item is done when all its done-probes pass (closed: PROACTIVE.md line + one ~/inbox/board-*.md note per tick);
a "move:SECTION" probe moves it once. No probe = "unverified" (shown in Due / In progress / Waiting on you).
Computed flags (never typed; stripped on import): " [board: overdue | due today | unverified]" at the line end.

TODO.md writes: the renderer owns TODO.md (snapshot before each write, the write only when the file is unchanged
after it was read, under its TODO lock; a render that would drop half the items is refused).
Asked: hooks append {"ts": epoch, "text": title} lines to ~/.local/state/board/asked.jsonl; every run drains it
(same matching as `board asked`) and prunes the entries of closed items. The feed rows carry created and asked.
State ~/.local/state/board/ (state.json, board.json = the dashboard feed, asked.jsonl, snapshots/, lock). Store: hubd
/board (hubboard.py, schemas/pg/004_board.sql). Env seams (tests): BOARD_STORE_FILE (a JSON store instead of the hub),
BOARD_TODO, BOARD_PROACTIVE, BOARD_INBOX, BOARD_STATE, BOARD_TODO_LOCK, BOARD_DEPLOYS,
BOARD_REPO, BOARD_BIN, BOARD_CMD_ALLOW, BOARD_TG_JOURNAL, BOARD_NOW (epoch or "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM"), BOARD_TZ.
Exit: 0 ok · 1 check failed / diff not clean · 2 bad input · 3 store unreachable · 4 refused (sanity, conflict).
"""
from __future__ import annotations

